        "original_id": "89cc0898-5354-568c-b267-51082f367c3e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Tritonia, Phyteuma, Zygotritonia\n- Taxonomy: genera, plant families, genus names\n- Places: Europe, Morocco\n\nFacts:\n- Tritonia is a genus of flowering plants in the iris family and was first described as a genus in 1802.\n- Phyteuma is a genus of flowering plants in the family Campanulaceae and is native to Europe and Morocco.\n- Zygotritonia is a genus whose name is derived from the word \"zygomorphic,\" meaning bilabiate, and from its apparent resemblance to some species in the genus Tritonia.",
